  "notes": "{混乱|こんらん} describes a state of disorder, confusion, or chaos. It can refer to mental confusion ({頭|あたま}が{混乱|こんらん}する) or situational chaos ({現場|げんば}が{混乱|こんらん}する).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {混乱|こんらん}する: to become confused/chaotic\n- {混乱|こんらん}が{生|しょう}じる: confusion arises\n- {混乱|こんらん}を{招|まね}く: to cause confusion\n- {混乱|こんらん}に{陥|おちい}る: to fall into chaos\n- {混乱|こんらん}を{収|おさ}める: to restore order\n- {大|おお}{混乱|こんらん}: great confusion\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed in both everyday and formal/news contexts. Common in reports about disasters, system failures, political upheaval, and schedule disruptions.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {騒動|そうどう}: commotion, disturbance (implies noise and activity)\n- パニック: panic (more extreme emotional response)\n- {混雑|こんざつ}: congestion, crowding (physical, not mental)",
